{
 "idea": {
  "id": "rev_no_news",
  "family": "reversal",
  "title": "Fade the week's moves only where there was no earnings report behind them",
  "why": "The reversal trade should work on moves made by pressure and fail on moves made by news, because news does not come back. Taking out stocks that reported in the window removes the largest known news days and should leave a cleaner trade (Da, Liu, Schaumburg 2014; Hameed and Mian 2015). The mirror variant fades only the stocks that did report, which should lose if the reasoning is right.",
